{"term":"loom","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:6ae5ad4253b8d9b80f","definition":"A utensil; tool; a weapon; (usually in compound) an article in general.","example":"heirloom, workloom","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["autoloom","backstrap loom","blessing loom","broadloom","drawloom","handloom","heirloom","hog-loom","hog loom","Jacquard loom","loom band","loomless","loom weight","loomworks","needle loom","power loom","satinet loom","warkloom","wiring loom","workloom"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/loom#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:d5e7104ed1e2f19a90","definition":"A frame or machine of wood or other material, in which a weaver forms cloth out of thread; a machine for interweaving yarn or threads into a fabric, as in knitting or lace making.","example":"January 8, 1751, Samuel Johnson, \"The Mischiefs of Total Idleness\" in The Rambler\nHector, when he sees Andromache overwhelmed with terror, sends her for consolation to the loom and the distaff.","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["autoloom","backstrap loom","blessing loom","broadloom","drawloom","handloom","heirloom","hog-loom","hog loom","Jacquard loom","loom band","loomless","loom weight","loomworks","needle loom","power loom","satinet loom","warkloom","wiring loom","workloom"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/loom#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:84807ce7e69a73efd0","definition":"The part of an oar which is between the grip or handle and the blade; the shaft.","example":"","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["autoloom","backstrap loom","blessing loom","broadloom","drawloom","handloom","heirloom","hog-loom","hog loom","Jacquard loom","loom band","loomless","loom weight","loomworks","needle loom","power loom","satinet loom","warkloom","wiring loom","workloom"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/loom#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:fbc84df9cef389dd41","definition":"loon (bird of order Gaviiformes)","example":"","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"dated","register":"dated","wordFamily":["autoloom","backstrap loom","blessing loom","broadloom","drawloom","handloom","heirloom","hog-loom","hog loom","Jacquard loom","loom band","loomless","loom weight","loomworks","needle loom","power loom","satinet loom","warkloom","wiring loom","workloom"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/loom#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:aa4a9597d04921a0df","definition":"To appear indistinctly, e.g. when seen on the horizon or through the murk.","example":"The clouds loomed over the mountains.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"intransitive","wordFamily":["autoloom","backstrap loom","blessing loom","broadloom","drawloom","handloom","heirloom","hog-loom","hog loom","Jacquard loom","loom band","loomless","loom weight","loomworks","needle loom","power loom","satinet loom","warkloom","wiring loom","workloom","loom ahead","loomingly","loom large","uploom"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/loom#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:9064822d8d9f1c17bb","definition":"To appear in an exaggerated or threatening form; (of a person or thing) to tower; (of an idea) to impressively or intimidatingly occupy the mind; (of an event) to be imminent.","example":"With no extra-time to be played and penalties looming, the Portuguese winger pounced on some hesitant City defending to run on to a Wayne Rooney clearance, round Joe Hart and slot home.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"figuratively","register":"figuratively, intransitive","wordFamily":["autoloom","backstrap loom","blessing loom","broadloom","drawloom","handloom","heirloom","hog-loom","hog loom","Jacquard loom","loom band","loomless","loom weight","loomworks","needle loom","power loom","satinet loom","warkloom","wiring loom","workloom","loom ahead","loomingly","loom large","uploom"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/loom#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:42994c3576853d8d10","definition":"To rise and to be eminent; to be elevated or ennobled, in a moral sense.","example":"On no occasion does he [Paul] loom so high, and shine so gloriously, as in the context.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"figuratively","register":"figuratively, intransitive","wordFamily":["autoloom","backstrap loom","blessing loom","broadloom","drawloom","handloom","heirloom","hog-loom","hog loom","Jacquard loom","loom band","loomless","loom weight","loomworks","needle loom","power loom","satinet loom","warkloom","wiring loom","workloom","loom ahead","loomingly","loom large","uploom"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/loom#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:95216b06d59550b8da","definition":"A distorted appearance of something as seen indistinctly or from afar.","example":"","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"intransitive","wordFamily":["autoloom","backstrap loom","blessing loom","broadloom","drawloom","handloom","heirloom","hog-loom","hog loom","Jacquard loom","loom ban